hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15828","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd al-Araj, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Rawahah, that he arrived from a journey at night and hastened to his wife, and there was a lamp in his house and with his wife was something, so he seized the sword. His wife said: Away from me, away from me; it is so-and-so combing my hair. So he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him, and he forbade a man to come to his family at night."
"15829","Yamar ibn Bishr narrated to us: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: I heard Sinan ibn Abi Sinan, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying, standing in his storytelling: A brother of yours who did not utter obscenity, meaning Ibn Rawahah, he said: And among us is the Messenger of Allah reciting His Book when a known brightness splits the night, he spends the night keeping his side away from his bed when the beds grow heavy with the disbelievers, he showed us guidance after blindness, so our hearts are certain through him that what he says is real."
